//sfcontroller.org/sites/default/files/Documents/Auditing/Give2SF%20Monthly%20Update%20Memorandum%2011.4.2020.pdf","sf":null},{"programme":"COVID-19 Emergency Family Relief Fund (2020-2021)","level":"local","administrator":"Human Rights Commission / OEWD (per Controller)","adults":"yes","children":"yes (families with children)","citation":"COVID-19 Disaster Family Relief Fund ordinance (2020) - text not retrieved","funding":"local (Give2SF donations; City reserves)","cost":"$4,884,000 Give2SF disbursements approved to community organizations","costWhere":"as of Nov 4, 2020, San Francisco","enrolment":"BOS member press release (Mar 18, 2021): \"$1000 to 4916 families\" to date; $2 million more","enrolmentWhere":"2020-Mar 2021, San Francisco","notes":"","source":"https://sfcontroller.org/sites/default/files/Documents/Auditing/Give2SF%20Monthly%20Update%20Memorandum%2011.4.2020.pdf","sf":null},{"programme":"Give2SF supportive services for immigrant workers / food security (2020)","level":"local","administrator":"Office of Civic Engagement and Immigrant Affairs; community grantees","adults":"yes","children":"yes","citation":"n/a (philanthropic fund administered by City)","funding":"local (Give2SF donations)","cost":"$115,000 per grant x4 (immigrant workers) and $100,000 x2 (food security) listed","costWhere":"as of Nov 4, 2020, San Francisco","enrolment":"","enrolmentWhere":"","notes":"","source":"https://sfcontroller.org/sites/default/files/Documents/Auditing/Give2SF%20Monthly%20Update%20Memorandum%2011.4.2020.pdf","sf":null},{"programme":"Immigrant legal defense and community response services","level":"local","administrator":"Mayor's Office of Housing and Community Development (Immigrant Legal Defense Collaborative); Public Defender Immigration Unit","adults":"yes (services not status-tested)","children":"yes","citation":"SF Ordinance No. 235-25 (FY2025-26 supplemental); SF Ordinance No. 132-25 (grant-funded Public Defender Immigration Defense Unit positions)","funding":"local (General Reserve); philanthropic grant for PD positions","cost":"$3,500,000 supplemental from General Reserve (in addition to base budget amounts not extracted)","costWhere":"FY 2025-26, San Francisco","enrolment":"","enrolmentWhere":"","notes":"","source":"https://www.sfbos.org/sites/default/files/o0235-25.pdf","sf":null},{"programme":"State immigration legal services (CDSS)","level":"state","administrator":"CDSS grants to nonprofits","adults":"yes (services)","children":"yes","citation":"Budget Act of 2026","funding":"state General Fund","cost":"$111.5 million one-time GF (increase)","costWhere":"2026-27, statewide","enrolment":"","enrolmentWhere":"","notes":"","source":"https://ebudget.ca.gov/2026-27/pdf/Enacted/BudgetSummary/HealthandHumanServices.pdf","sf":null}],"findings":[{"date":"2017-01","body":"HHS Office of Inspector General (A-09-15-02020)","programme":"Medicaid (Medi-Cal)","found":"\"California did not correctly identify all nonreimbursable claims for nonemergency services provided to qualified aliens, resulting in $9.9 million in unallowable Federal Medicaid reimbursement over 5 years.\" (qualified aliens within the 5-year waiting period; MMIS error when claims approved in one quarter and paid in a later quarter)","amountText":"$9,872,618 Federal share","amount":9872618,"period":"quarters ended June 2010, Sept 2010, June 2011, June 2012, June 2013, June 2014","response":"State agency \"partially agreed\" with refund recommendation (agreed to refund but said amount overstated because pregnant women and children are not subject to the 5-year bar); agreed with the other two recommendations","status":"not stated in retrieved files (OIG Recommendation Tracker returned \"No results\" for this report number)","notes":"Concerns qualified aliens under the 5-year bar, not undocumented immigrants.","source":"https://oig.hhs.gov/documents/audit/9415/A-09-15-02020-Complete%20Report.pdf","aboutStatus":false,"kind":"audit or federal action"},{"date":"2018-12","body":"HHS Office of Inspector General (A-09-17-02002)","programme":"Medicaid (Medi-Cal) non-newly eligible group","found":"Of 125 sampled beneficiaries, payments were made on behalf of 65 ineligible or potentially ineligible beneficiaries; one sampled beneficiary \"did not meet the citizenship requirement\". Overall estimate: $959.3 million ($536 million Federal share) for 802,742 ineligible beneficiaries and $4.5 billion ($2.6 billion Federal share) for 3.1 million potentially ineligible beneficiaries (all causes)","amountText":"estimate for all eligibility errors; citizenship component not separately estimated","amount":null,"period":"services Oct 2014 - Mar 2015","response":"\"California agreed with our findings. California partly agreed with our recommendation regarding beneficiaries determined eligible for Medicaid based on eligibility for another assistance program\"; did not explicitly agree or disagree with other recommendations","status":"not stated in retrieved files","notes":"Citizenship is one of several error types; only 1 of 125 sampled cases.","source":"https://oig.hhs.gov/documents/audit/9474/A-09-17-02002-Complete%20Report.pdf","aboutStatus":true,"kind":"audit or federal action"},{"date":"2020","body":"Centers for Medicare & Medicaid Services","programme":"Medi-Cal","found":"CMS letter (3/18/2025): \"In 2020, CMS discovered that California, by its own admission, had been erroneously claiming significant amounts of federal Medicaid funds for individuals without a satisfactory immigration status. As a result of this discovery, CMS initiated immediate action through the regulatory deferral process to withhold FFP\"; deferrals \"on a quarterly basis\"","amountText":"not stated","amount":null,"period":"2020 onward","response":"per CMS, state self-reported (\"by its own admission\")","status":"deferrals continuing (see 2026-05-13 rows)","notes":"Individual quarterly deferral letters before FFY 2026 Q1 not retrieved.","source":"https://kff.org/wp-content/uploads/sites/3/2025/08/CA-Letter-FFP-for-Undocumented.pdf","aboutStatus":true,"kind":"audit or federal action"},{"date":"2023-09","body":"Centers for Medicare & Medicaid Services (Financial Management Review)","programme":"Medi-Cal fee-for-service","found":"CMS FMR \"of California's claiming of FFP relating to certain fee-for-service services provided during the review period to individuals not in a satisfactory immigration status ... identified $34.1 million FFP in overpayments\"; also \"recommended state corrective action on a variety of state internal controls and state systems issues\"","amountText":"$34.1 million FFP","amount":34100000,"period":"review period not stated in letter","response":"\"The state has returned the overpayments to CMS.\"","status":"overpayments returned (per CMS)","notes":"FMR report itself not retrieved.","source":"https://kff.org/wp-content/uploads/sites/3/2025/08/CA-Letter-FFP-for-Undocumented.pdf","aboutStatus":true,"kind":"audit or federal action"},{"date":"2024-05-17","body":"HHS Office of Inspector General (A-09-22-02004)","programme":"Medi-Cal managed care capitation","found":"\"California improperly claimed $52.7 million in Federal Medicaid reimbursement because it continued to use the proxy percentage that was developed in the early 2000s\"; proxy 39.87% vs OIG-calculated 48.36% for nonemergency services to noncitizens with UIS","amountText":"$52,652,689 Federal share (of $372.9 million Federal share audited; $888.8 million total)","amount":52652689,"period":"Oct 1, 2018 - June 30, 2019","response":"California \"partially concurred\" with refund recommendation (\"does not contest the recommendation but ... is unable to replicate or concur with our recalculated proxy percentage\"; proposed manual return) and concurred with the second","status":"Rec 24-A-09-076.01 \"Closed Implemented\" 08/25/2024; Rec 24-A-09-076.02 \"Closed Acceptable Alternative\" 06/05/2025 (tracker last updated Oct 26, 2026)","notes":"CMS requested this audit.","source":"https://oig.hhs.gov/documents/audit/9894/A-09-22-02004.pdf","aboutStatus":true,"kind":"audit or federal action"},{"date":"2025-03-18","body":"Centers for Medicare & Medicaid Services (letter to State Medicaid Director)","programme":"Medi-Cal","found":"\"To date, CMS has collected over $500 million FFP for overpayments identified outside of the review period of the FMR and OIG audit\"; CMS \"intends to conduct additional oversight activities\" including possible \"deferral or disallowance of FFP\" and \"possible referrals to the Attorney General\"","amountText":"over $500 million FFP collected","amount":500000000,"period":"not stated","response":"state response not retrieved (DHCS site behind bot challenge)","status":"oversight continuing","notes":"Copy hosted by KFF; no cms.gov original located.","source":"https://kff.org/wp-content/uploads/sites/3/2025/08/CA-Letter-FFP-for-Undocumented.pdf","aboutStatus":false,"kind":"audit or federal action"},{"date":"2025-05-27","body":"Centers for Medicare & Medicaid Services (press release and letter to all states)","programme":"Medicaid (all states)","found":"announced \"increased federal oversight to stop states from misusing federal Medicaid dollars to cover health care for individuals who are in the country illegally\": focused evaluations of CMS-64 submissions, reviews of financial management systems; \"Any improper spending on noncitizens will be subject to recoupment of the federal share.\"","amountText":"n/a","amount":null,"period":"n/a","response":"","status":"policy announcement","notes":"Not California-specific.","source":"https://www.cms.gov/newsroom/press-releases/cms-increasing-oversight-states-illegally-using-federal-medicaid-funding-health-care-illegal","aboutStatus":true,"kind":"rule or notice"},{"date":"2025-07-10","body":"U.S. Department of Agriculture (Federal Register notice 90 FR 30621)","programme":"programmes re-classified as \"Federal public benefit\" under PRWORA","found":"notice interpreting/specifying which programmes are \"Federal public benefits\" subject to 8 USC 1611 verification and eligibility limits (see notice text)","amountText":"n/a","amount":null,"period":"n/a","response":"court challenges not researched/retrieved","status":"see notice; current status not verified","notes":"","source":"https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/FR-2025-07-10/pdf/2025-12691.pdf","aboutStatus":true,"kind":"rule or notice"},{"date":"2025-07-11","body":"U.S. Department of Education (Federal Register notice 90 FR 30896)","programme":"programmes re-classified as \"Federal public benefit\" under PRWORA","found":"notice interpreting/specifying which programmes are \"Federal public benefits\" subject to 8 USC 1611 verification and eligibility limits (see notice text)","amountText":"n/a","amount":null,"period":"n/a","response":"court challenges not researched/retrieved","status":"see notice; current status not verified","notes":"","source":"https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/FR-2025-07-11/pdf/2025-12925.pdf","aboutStatus":true,"kind":"rule or notice"},{"date":"2025-07-14","body":"U.S. Department of Health and Human Services (Federal Register notice 90 FR 31232)","programme":"programmes re-classified as \"Federal public benefit\" under PRWORA","found":"notice interpreting/specifying which programmes are \"Federal public benefits\" subject to 8 USC 1611 verification and eligibility limits (see notice text)","amountText":"n/a","amount":null,"period":"n/a","response":"court challenges not researched/retrieved","status":"see notice; current status not verified","notes":"","source":"https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/FR-2025-07-14/pdf/2025-13118.pdf","aboutStatus":true,"kind":"rule or notice"},{"date":"2025-07-16","body":"U.S. Department of Justice (Federal Register notice 90 FR 32023)","programme":"programmes re-classified as \"Federal public benefit\" under PRWORA","found":"notice interpreting/specifying which programmes are \"Federal public benefits\" subject to 8 USC 1611 verification and eligibility limits (see notice text)","amountText":"n/a","amount":null,"period":"n/a","response":"court challenges not researched/retrieved","status":"see notice; current status not verified","notes":"","source":"https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/FR-2025-07-16/pdf/2025-13318.pdf","aboutStatus":true,"kind":"rule or notice"},{"date":"2025-09 (FY2023 report)","body":"USDA Food and Nutrition Service (SNAP Quality Control)","programme":"SNAP / CalFresh","found":"FY2023 QC Table 21 \"Benefit and Error Dollars by Citizenship Status of Participants\": California households with non-citizens = 24.24% of benefits and 26.25% of error dollars (U.S. average 14.28% / 14.25%). FY2025 California payment error rate 10.93% (overpayments 10.06%, underpayments 0.87%)","amountText":"n/a (shares)","amount":null,"period":"FY2023; FY2025","response":"","status":"published statistic","notes":"Not an element-level finding: error dollars by the \"citizenship and non-citizen status\" element are not published by state in these reports (only in case-level QC microdata, deliberately not downloaded). FY2022 Table 21 shows 0.00 for California as published. LAO 5208 part 3: under H.R. 1 \"the state will become liable for share of CalFresh benefit costs totaling as much as $2 billion annually beginning October 2027 if it does not significantly reduce its payment error rate.\"","source":"https://www.fna.usda.gov/sites/default/files/resource-files/snap-qc-annualreportfy23.pdf","aboutStatus":true,"kind":"audit or federal action"},{"date":"2025-11-26","body":"U.S. Department of Housing and Urban Development (Federal Register notice 90 FR 54363)","programme":"programmes re-classified as \"Federal public benefit\" under PRWORA","found":"notice interpreting/specifying which programmes are \"Federal public benefits\" subject to 8 USC 1611 verification and eligibility limits (see notice text)","amountText":"n/a","amount":null,"period":"n/a","response":"court challenges not researched/retrieved","status":"see notice; current status not verified","notes":"","source":"https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/FR-2025-11-26/pdf/2025-21120.pdf","aboutStatus":true,"kind":"rule or notice"},{"date":"2026 (in progress)","body":"California State Auditor (2025-604)","programme":"Medi-Cal eligibility","found":"High-risk audit of DHCS Medi-Cal eligibility; objective: \"Evaluate trends in the number and type of Medi-Cal eligibility discrepancies. To the extent possible, determine the amount of questionable costs associated with these discrepancies.\"","amountText":"n/a","amount":null,"period":"n/a","response":"","status":"Status: \"In progress\"; \"Est. Release Date: Winter 2026-27\"","notes":"No State Auditor report specific to immigration-status claiming was found; 2025-601 and 2020-613 concern Medi-Cal eligibility generally.","source":"https://www.auditor.ca.gov/wp-content/uploads/2026/03/2025-604-Audit-Scope-and-Objectives.pdf","aboutStatus":false,"kind":"audit or federal action"},{"date":"2026-01-23","body":"U.S. Department of Housing and Urban Development (with DHS)","programme":"HUD-assisted housing (national)","found":"\"Following a ... HUD and DHS audit into all tenants across HUD-funded housing nationwide, HUD discovered nearly 200,000 tenants requiring eligibility verification, nearly 25,000 deceased tenants, and nearly 6,000 ineligible non-American tenants\"; PHAs and owners given 30 days to review EIV-SAVE Tenant Match Report; \"HUD will recapture funding for payments made on behalf of ineligible\" tenants","amountText":"not stated","amount":null,"period":"not stated","response":"","status":"directive issued; SF-specific results not published in retrieved files","notes":"HUD FAQ: PHAs \"cannot use the SAVE initial status in the report alone\" to find someone ineligible.","source":"https://www.hud.gov/news/hud-no-26-008","aboutStatus":false,"kind":"rule or notice"},{"date":"2026-02","body":"California Legislative Analyst's Office (LAO 5146)","programme":"Medi-Cal","found":"\"General Fund spending is $1.4 billion higher ... Much of the increase in General Fund spending is due to higher repayments to the federal government. These repayments generally reflect corrections to erroneous federal claiming for state-only services provided to enrollees with unsatisfactory immigration status (UIS).\"","amountText":"$1.4 billion higher GF in 2025-26 (repayments are \"much of\" it; not separately quantified)","amount":1400000000,"period":"2025-26","response":"","status":"reflected in state budget","notes":"LAO description of Governor's Budget estimate, not an audit finding.","source":"https://lao.ca.gov/reports/2026/5146/2026-27_Medi-Cal_Analysis_030226.pdf","aboutStatus":true,"kind":"audit or federal action"},{"date":"2026-03-05","body":"U.S. Department of Housing and Urban Development (Notice PIH 2026-05)","programme":"Emergency Housing Vouchers / Stability Vouchers","found":"Notice \"strikes the following waiver and alternative requirement related to the verification of citizenship or eligible immigration status\" from the EHV and SV notices","amountText":"n/a","amount":null,"period":"n/a","response":"","status":"in effect","notes":"","source":"https://www.hud.gov/sites/default/files/PIH/documents/PIH-2026-05.pdf","aboutStatus":true,"kind":"rule or notice"},{"date":"2026-05-13","body":"Centers for Medicare & Medicaid Services (deferral CA/2026/1/E/03/MAP)","programme":"Medi-Cal","found":"\"repeat deferral for drug rebates that have not been returned for the UIS population ... This is the 25th repeat deferral, bringing the total deferred FFP on this issue to $120,195,149.\"","amountText":"$7,294,000 FFP deferred this quarter; $120,195,149 cumulative","amount":7294000,"period":"CMS-64 quarter ended Dec 31, 2025 (FFY 2026 Q1)","response":"CMS: within 60 days provide documentation or make decreasing adjustment on Line 10B of CMS-64 for quarter ended Mar 31, 2026","status":"deferred (withheld pending documentation)","notes":"","source":"https://www.cms.gov/files/document/deferral-letter-ca-q1-2026.pdf","aboutStatus":true,"kind":"audit or federal action"},{"date":"2026-05-13","body":"Centers for Medicare & Medicaid Services (deferral CA/2026/1/E/04/MAP)","programme":"Medi-Cal supplemental payments","found":"\"repeat deferral for Medi-Cal supplemental payment programs that included UIS unallowable services or UIS population data in the calculation of costs\"; deferral computed after \"the state's voluntary reduction of $28,103,621\"","amountText":"$3,876,387 FFP","amount":3876387,"period":"CMS-64 quarter ended Dec 31, 2025 (FFY 2026 Q1)","response":"CMS: within 60 days provide documentation or make decreasing adjustment on Line 10B of CMS-64 for quarter ended Mar 31, 2026","status":"deferred","notes":"","source":"https://www.cms.gov/files/document/deferral-letter-ca-q1-2026.pdf","aboutStatus":true,"kind":"audit or federal action"},{"date":"2026-05-13","body":"Centers for Medicare & Medicaid Services (deferral CA/2026/1/E/07/MAP)","programme":"Medi-Cal fee-for-service","found":"\"repeat deferral for FFS medical claims submitted for the individuals lacking satisfactory immigration status, which appear not to meet the state's criteria for emergency services\"","amountText":"$126,735 FFP","amount":126735,"period":"CMS-64 quarter ended Dec 31, 2025 (FFY 2026 Q1)","response":"CMS: within 60 days provide documentation or make decreasing adjustment on Line 10B of CMS-64 for quarter ended Mar 31, 2026","status":"deferred","notes":"","source":"https://www.cms.gov/files/document/deferral-letter-ca-q1-2026.pdf","aboutStatus":true,"kind":"audit or federal action"},{"date":"2026-05-13","body":"Centers for Medicare & Medicaid Services (deferral CA/2026/1/E/08/ADM)","programme":"Medi-Cal administration","found":"\"repeat deferral based on the May 30, 2025, letter CMS received from the state indicating the state has initiated a comprehensive review of its methodology and systems for allocating and claiming Medicaid administrative costs related to state-only funded services\"; 15% reduction against excluded costs","amountText":"$130,560,068 FFP","amount":130560068,"period":"CMS-64 quarter ended Dec 31, 2025 (FFY 2026 Q1)","response":"CMS: within 60 days provide documentation or make decreasing adjustment on Line 10B of CMS-64 for quarter ended Mar 31, 2026","status":"deferred","notes":"Concerns state-only funded services generally (the letter does not limit this item to UIS).","source":"https://www.cms.gov/files/document/deferral-letter-ca-q1-2026.pdf","aboutStatus":true,"kind":"audit or federal action"},{"date":"2026-05-13","body":"Centers for Medicare & Medicaid Services (deferral CA/2026/1/E/09/MAP)","programme":"Medi-Cal emergency services","found":"\"new deferral for the services claimed as UIS emergency care solely based on the presence of weeks gestation of pregnancy-related codes\"; state asked to reclassify not-time-barred claims to Title XXI","amountText":"$4,638,583 FFP","amount":4638583,"period":"CMS-64 quarter ended Dec 31, 2025 (FFY 2026 Q1)","response":"CMS: within 60 days provide documentation or make decreasing adjustment on Line 10B of CMS-64 for quarter ended Mar 31, 2026","status":"deferred","notes":"Same letter also deferred non-UIS items: CFC-PCS $1,133,487,260; Group VIII age-mismatch $23,100,437; IMD $8,000,000; overstated admin costs $32,377,507; eligibility mismatches $220,911 and $30,086.","source":"https://www.cms.gov/files/document/deferral-letter-ca-q1-2026.pdf","aboutStatus":true,"kind":"audit or federal action"},{"date":"2026-11-12","body":"U.S. Department of Housing and Urban Development (final rule, 91 FR 72978)","programme":"Section 214 covered programs (public housing, Section 8)","found":"final rule requires \"verification of U.S. citizenship or the eligible immigration status of all applicants and recipients ... regardless of age\" and makes \"prorated assistance a temporary condition pending verification of eligible status of a